(c) 2012-2013 Chris Patuzzo, MVP (Microsoft Valued Professional)# Election_Analysis

## Project Overview
The purpose of this project is to assist a Colorado Board of Elections employee in conducting an audit of a recent local congressional election. We will use Python to automate the process and generate the following 6 key deliverables:

1) Calculate the total number of votes cast.
2) Get a complete list of candidates who received votes.
3) Calculate the total number of votes each candidate received.
4) Calculate the percentage of votes each candidate received.
5) Determine the winner of the election based on popular vote.

## Resources
Data Source: election_results.csv
Software: Python 3.7, Visual Studio Code 1.44

## Summary
The analysis of the election showcased that:

- There were a total of 369,711 votes cast in the election
- The candidates were Charles Casper Stockham, Diana DeGette, and Raymon Anthony Doane
- Charles Casper Stockham received 23.0% of the total votes, with 85,213 votes. 
- Diana Degette received 73.8% of the total votes, with 272,892 votes.
- Raymon Anthony Doane received 3.1% of the total votes, with 11,606 votes.
- The winner of the election was Diana Degette, who received 73.8% of the votes and 272,892 votes

## Challenge Overview
The purpose of this challenge was to take an existing piece of Python code and make it more dynamic. In this case, the user can input any small or large csv data file by changing the pathname ("election_results.csv") and the output files will be named automatically as "analysis_results.txt" and "summary_result.txt". If the csv file has a different format, the code will automatically adjust to accommodate that (for instance, different column positions for county and candidate names, different delimiters, etc.) 
![Screen Shot 2022-02-17 at 4 48 23 PM](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/88928155/154471415-0d181f48-c8d6-4591-b2d5-a6809b754548.png)

## Challenge Summary
The code has successfully read the elections data csv file, processed it, calculated all the necessary stats and provided the results in a neat and organized table that can be easily understood. The output tables include the percentage of total votes for each candidate as well as the overall winner of the election based on popular vote. The final analysis and summary tables have also been exported to text files for convenient viewing and further analysis.

## Recommendations for Future Use
The code can be utilized for any future elections by importing the main function "analyze_and_export_election_data" from the "election_analysis.py" python script. This function has three parameters: "csv_file_path", "analysis_results_txt_file_path", and "summary_result_txt_file_path". Subsequently, one can call this function specifying the appropriate file path of the elections data csv, as well as where to store the analysis and summary results text files.

For instance:

